You seem to think that it somehow takes fewer bits to describe a
quantum state of the universe that to describe a classical state.
Thus if the VR simulators are trying to save on bits, they'd rather
choose quantum physics.  But this just isn't so, to my knowledge.  A
simulation with a finite number of bits would eventually have to
diverge from the exact physics, and I don't know why that divergence
should be harder to detect for quantum physics.

