Subject: CHAT: Deadly puns

What's a cryptographer?  A person who decodes the mysteries of death.

OK, so maybe it's not very funny, but it is rather apt.  I noticed the
"crypt" in "cryptography" earlier today when I posted the news about random
number generators.  Later, upon consulting my dictionary, I discovered that
both words derive from the Greek "kryptos," which means "hidden."  So one
might say that cryonicists perform cryogenic cryptography!

(But note that the similarity between cryonics/cryogenics and
crypt/cryptography is pure happenstance.  The former two terms come from
the Greek "kryos," for "frost"--not from the "kryptos" that gives rise to
the latter two terms.)




